"}], "explanation": "The previous fix freed oldData unconditionally after a successful realloc, which caused a double-free/use-after-free when realloc returned the same pointer (in-place growth). Now oldData is only freed when realloc returned a different pointer, and it is freed if realloc fails. This preserves output ("5", "10") and eliminates the leak."}
